    "equivalent": true,
    "why": "The scan runs top-down: a rung whose rung above stands out from it by less than the inset is only reached once that rung above was itself asked and refused - and what refuses it (no step of its own above it, no depth up the rungs over it) leaves this rung's own depth walk short too. Kept so the top's probe, the inset past the face from the rung above, never starts inside the wall."
